Negative control for the FE-3113 offer/gap spec (`AC5`).

`captureGaps` bills a module for a missing capture only where its `.feature`
DECLARES the refusal, read off the scenario tags. The mutant re-adds the prose
gate the story deleted, as a fallback beside the tag read — so a feature is
billed for wording a failure anywhere in its English, and every module whose
prose says "error" once owes a capture it never declared. The tag path is left
intact, so nothing an honest declaration reports is withdrawn: only false debt is
added.

What must go red is the DIRECTION of a false gap. An assertion that only checks a
declaring module reports its gap passes the mutant unchanged, because the mutant
never under-reports — it over-reports. Sweep the modules that declare NO refusal
and require an empty report from each; a single one of them named is the whole
finding.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the answerable-presets spec — bills only a feature that DECLARES the
refusal, and owes no capture anywhere in the tree today.

Re-armed 2026-08-31: the tag-read moved into hostablePresets; the mutant
re-adds the deleted prose gate beside it.

